 "story": {
  "kicker": "Seventh Ward",
  "h2": "Tastee Restaurant Deli-Donuts",
  "paragraphs": [
   "Tastee is the pink building on Esplanade with the brown metal roof and a row of yellow bollards planted along the front. A neon HAMBURGER sign burns in one window. In the other there is a paper sign taped to the glass that spells the whole operation out: Mon to Sat 5am to 5pm, Sunday 5am to 1pm. Inside it is red tile floor, a counter with stools, and glass racks of donuts running the length of it.",
   "The donuts are the headline. Glazed at ninety-two cents, filled and cake a little over a dollar, apple fritters and cinnamon rolls in their own trays, and the shoesole, a long flat glazed pastry that is the one regulars reach for. A dozen glazed is $8.49. The board behind the counter has held those numbers long enough that people quote them."
  ]
 },
 "facts": [
  "Dine in at the counter, takeout, or delivery",
